{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:d34674a1187e91cd","name":"Starship Maneuvers","source":{"id":"source:reference-d34674a1187e91cd","title":"Starship Maneuvers","revision":18810,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:46:17Z","sha256":"12274e530a43cb30dec3264f42d88aacb9775921a13b651f09a9f9aadd50f85b","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18810","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Starship%20Maneuvers&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-d34674a1187e91cd","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Starship Maneuvers system provides new options for any character acting as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," during a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"}," encounter. Similar to the system for using ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Powers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Powers","referenceId":"reference:85acec94cd1ca5f3"},", the Starship Maneuvers system allows characters to perform incredible stunts or make use of advanced tactics in order to gain the upper hand in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"}," combat. Except for Starship Maneuvers used by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunners"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunners"},", only ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilots"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilots"}," of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeders","referenceId":"reference:8831ac17fd67f6fc"}," may make use of the mechanics in this section- ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transports"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transports","referenceId":"reference:082a04e1f80578b3"}," are too large and cumbersome. (However, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Combat Thrusters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Combat_Thrusters","referenceId":"reference:67aecd921f38dbd3"}," Starship Modification may be used on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transports"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transports","referenceId":"reference:082a04e1f80578b3"}," to circumvent this restriction).\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A Starship Maneuver is a special action that allows a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," to do something beyond the bounds of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," skill and the abilities provided by the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ace Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ace_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:3c2fd5c8fcea1d9d"}," Prestige Class. Starship Maneuvers enhance attacks, strengthen defenses, reduce damage, or produce other unique effects. A character who takes the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Tactics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Tactics","referenceId":"reference:f78ca765752eb7c6"}," feat automatically learns a number of Starship Maneuvers equal to 1 + their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wisdom"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wisdom"}," modifier (minimum of 1). A character can learn additional Starship Maneuvers by taking the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Tactics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Tactics","referenceId":"reference:f78ca765752eb7c6"}," feat again or by increasing their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wisdom"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wisdom"}," modifier.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["For example, Syal Antilles is a 5th-level ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," with a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wisdom"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wisdom"}," score of 13 (+1 modifier). When she advances to 6th level, she takes the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Tactics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Tactics","referenceId":"reference:f78ca765752eb7c6"}," feat and immediately gains two Starship Maneuvers. She chooses ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Attack Pattern Delta"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attack_Pattern_Delta","referenceId":"reference:6fa920ff189c0f3c"}]}," and ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Corellian Slip"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Corellian_Slip","referenceId":"reference:7d8e80ae2ae48dd2"}]},". At 8th level, Syal raises her ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wisdom"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wisdom"}," score from 13 to 14, thereby increasing her ability modifier from +1 to +2; at that time, she gains an additional Starship Maneuver (since she has taken the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Tactics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Tactics","referenceId":"reference:f78ca765752eb7c6"}," feat once); she chooses ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Target Lock"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Target_Lock","referenceId":"reference:ac59d88c386d66a0"}]},". At 9th level, Syal selects the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Tactics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Tactics","referenceId":"reference:f78ca765752eb7c6"}," feat again, granting her three new Starship Maneuvers. She chooses ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Tallon Roll"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tallon_Roll","referenceId":"reference:14cb5e3d07ff9587"}]},", ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Angle Deflector Shields"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Angle_Deflector_Shields","referenceId":"reference:438b0255a92258fb"}]},", and a second use of ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Corellian Slip"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Corellian_Slip","referenceId":"reference:7d8e80ae2ae48dd2"}]},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Starship Maneuvers in Your Game"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Adding the Starship Maneuvers system to your game can greatly change it, so Gamemasters should feel free to allow or disallow this system as fits their campaign. Taking the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Tactics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Tactics","referenceId":"reference:f78ca765752eb7c6"}," Feat consumes a valuable ",{"tag":"a","children":["Feat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Feat"}," slot, so players should likely do so only if the campaign features a good amount of space or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeder"}," combat. A good rule of thumb is that if the player won't have a chance to use any of these Starship Maneuvers at least once per adventure, the Gamemaster should seriously consider whether to allow the Starship Maneuvers system in the game.\n"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Starship Maneuver Suite"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Your character's Starship Maneuvers collectively form a suite. When your character uses a Starship Maneuver, that Starship Maneuver is spent and is no longer available for use by your character until it is recovered. You may have multiple uses of the same Starship Maneuver in your Starship Maneuver Suite.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When your character uses a Starship Maneuver, make a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," check. The check result determines the Starship Maneuver's result. Most Starship Maneuvers have varying degrees of success, but some (including all Starship Maneuvers with the [",{"tag":"i","children":["Attack Pattern"]},"] descriptor) have an all-or-nothing effect. For those with multitiered effects, your check result determines the maximum effect you can achieve, though you can also choose a lesser effect. If your check result is too low to activate the Starship Maneuver's most basic effect, nothing happens, the Starship Maneuver is spent, and the Action is wasted.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["You have different ways to regain spent Starship Maneuvers, making them available for use once more.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["When a combat sequence is over and you have a chance to rest for 1 minute, you regain all Starship Maneuvers."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["If you roll a Natural 20 on a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," check made to activate a Starship Maneuver (but not for any other uses of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," skill), you regain all spent Starship Maneuvers at the end of your turn."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["You can spend a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Point"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Point"}," as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reaction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reaction"}," and immediately regain one spent Starship Maneuver."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["Some unique abilities allow you to regain spent Starship Maneuvers in other ways."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Starship Maneuver Descriptors"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Some Starship Maneuvers fall into special categories that affect how they are used and who can use them. The following descriptors are applied to any relevant Starship Maneuvers mentioned in this section:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Attack Pattern"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Starship Maneuvers that have the [",{"tag":"i","children":["Attack Pattern"]},"] descriptor represent formations and flying patterns that form an overall combat strategy. An [",{"tag":"i","children":["Attack Pattern"]},"] Starship Maneuver differs from other maneuvers in that, once activated, its effects last until the end of the encounter. Additionally, you may gain the benefit from only one [",{"tag":"i","children":["Attack Pattern"]},"] Starship Maneuver at a time, and if you activate an [",{"tag":"i","children":["Attack Pattern"]},"] Starship Maneuver while already gaining the benefits of another, the second Starship Maneuver replaces the effects of the first.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Dogfight"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Starship Maneuvers that have the [",{"tag":"i","children":["Dogfight"]},"] descriptor represent tactics and actions that apply only in close combat situations. A [",{"tag":"i","children":["Dogfight"]},"] Starship Maneuver may only be activated while your ship is engaged in a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dogfight"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dogfight","referenceId":"reference:d47b1a4208bcd07f"}," with another ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," or group of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Force"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A Starship Maneuver that has the [",{"tag":"i","children":["Force"]},"] descriptor is one that relies on the user's connection to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," for its benefit. Only characters who are ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trained"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained"}," in the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," skill may make use of [",{"tag":"i","children":["Force"]},"] Starship Maneuvers, and activating a [",{"tag":"i","children":["Force"]},"] Starship Maneuver is considered using ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Gunner"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A Starship Maneuver that has the [",{"tag":"i","children":["Gunner"]},"] descriptor does not require you to be the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," of the ship in order to activate. Any [",{"tag":"i","children":["Gunner"]},"] Starship Maneuvers may be activated by either the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Copilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Copilot","referenceId":"reference:49f5b0e488cfa66c"}," (using ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Copilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Copilot","referenceId":"reference:49f5b0e488cfa66c"},"-controlled ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Systems"},") or by a character serving as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," aboard a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeder"},".\n"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Core Starship Maneuvers"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["STARSHIP MANEUVER\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["TYPE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["TIME REQUIREMENT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["DESCRIPTION\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Ackbar Slash"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ackbar_Slash","referenceId":"reference:707db1e318f7ea10"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["N/A\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reaction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reaction"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["A starship tactic made famous by the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mon Calamari"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mon_Calamari","referenceId":"reference:5b784aed2214627b"}," Admiral Ackbar, the ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Ackbar Slash"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ackbar_Slash","referenceId":"reference:707db1e318f7ea10"}]}," involves a ship moving into the midst of enemy forces in order to cause an opponent to strike its own allies.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Afterburn"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Afterburn","referenceId":"reference:61c4e59ad497de0e"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["N/A\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Action"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["This maneuver allows a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," to throttle up and blast past enemies, to avoid becoming entangled in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dogfights"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dogfights"},".\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Angle Deflector Shields"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Angle_Deflector_Shields","referenceId":"reference:438b0255a92258fb"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Attack Pattern"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["This Attack Pattern focuses deflector shields in a particular direction, making it easier to absorb incoming attacks from a certain angle.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Attack Formation Zeta Nine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attack_Formation_Zeta_Nine","referenceId":"reference:e8b8fb4fc1cb1b3d"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Attack Pattern"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["This Attack Pattern is typically used to approach ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," or other vessels that have heavy firepower. It emphasizes the role of shields over firepower.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Attack Pattern Delta"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attack_Pattern_Delta","referenceId":"reference:6fa920ff189c0f3c"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Attack Pattern"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["This Attack Pattern utilizes close-range maneuvering by allied ships to make it more difficult to target and hit an individual vessel. The Attack Pattern typically requires the vessels to fly in a straight line toward their target, shielding the ships to the rear.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Corellian Slip"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Corellian_Slip","referenceId":"reference:7d8e80ae2ae48dd2"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["N/A\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Action"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["A teamwork-focused ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," tactic, the ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Corellian Slip"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Corellian_Slip","referenceId":"reference:7d8e80ae2ae48dd2"}]}," maneuver allows a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," to destroy an opposing Starship that threatens one of his or her allies by flying at the enemy vessel head-on.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Counter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Counter","referenceId":"reference:a78cfdf4acfc2942"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Dogfight"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reaction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reaction"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["This maneuver allows a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," to take a quick action while engaged in a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dogfight"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dogfight","referenceId":"reference:d47b1a4208bcd07f"}," after being the target of an attack.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Darklighter Spin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darklighter_Spin","referenceId":"reference:b5f2fe685829889c"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["N/A\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Originally an improvised combat maneuver, the ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Darklighter Spin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darklighter_Spin","referenceId":"reference:b5f2fe685829889c"}]}," maneuver allows you to attack multiple targets with your Starship's weapons.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Devastating Hit"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Devastating_Hit","referenceId":"reference:31a12da1dd155cc3"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Gunner"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["This maneuver lets you score an incredibly precise hit on the target, punching holes in vital systems and potentially disabling your target.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Engine Hit"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Engine_Hit","referenceId":"reference:dc22aa4edb5543d2"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Gunner"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reaction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reaction"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["This maneuver allows you to target an opponent's engines, slowing them down with a successful hit.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Evasive Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Evasive_Action","r